  "verbalization": "Pethidine, as part of the Full Opioid Agonists class, binds to Oprm1 through a shared mechanism that involves opioid receptor activation. This is supported by the evidence that Pethidine, along with its analogs like Remifentanil, Dihydrocodeine, and Sufentanil, all bind to the Oprm1 receptor. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds—Opioid Receptor Agonist and Piperidines—highlight a common pathway in their interaction with the receptor. The presence of these shared ancestors suggests that the binding to Oprm1 is mediated by a common structural feature, likely the opioid receptor binding domain. The evidence from the three paths collectively supports the notion that Pethidine and Oprm1 are linked through a shared pharmacological mechanism, emphasizing the role of opioid receptor agonism in their interaction.",
